    {
      "type": "evidence",
      "id": "evidence",
      "title": "Why trust me with it.",
      "intro": "Design systems are where most of my career has been spent.",
      "items": [
        {
          "claim": "I was building [design.orange.com](https://design.orange.com) before anyone called it a design system",
          "proof": "Much of my 20+ years in enterprise UX and design systems was spent building them inside Orange, one of Europe's largest telecoms groups.",
          "source": "From [oganiko.com](https://oganiko.com)"
        },
        {
          "claim": "Knowing when a system needs a new home",
          "proof": "When Orange's design system outgrew its WordPress platform, I led its move to a dedicated documentation tool, before it became a problem.",
          "source": "From the WordPress story on [oganiko.com](https://oganiko.com)"
        },
        {
          "claim": "A design system starts with who it's for",
          "proof": "For STR Technologies and mAbV, background research showed the audience is primarily scientists. The personas went into each design system and set its rules: a clean, clinical white throughout, and no dark mode, which has no place in the world of biochemistry.",
          "source": "[STR design system](https://str-design-system.web.app/styleguide/) · [mAbV design system](https://mabvbio.com/design-system/)"
        },
        {
          "claim": "My own system runs every site I build",
          "proof": "The OGANIKO Design System: tokens in one source file generate the code, every component carries a maturity status, and a check fails when the output drifts from the source.",
          "source": "From [oganiko.com](https://oganiko.com)"
        }
      ]
    },
