      "label": "From what exists to a system teams use",
      "title": "From mess to system.",
      "intro": "How I build a design system: start from who it's for and what your products already have, agree the foundations with your teams, then document it and roll it out one product at a time.",
      "groupLabel": "↺ Review with your teams until it's right",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Who it's for",
          "text": "Research the people your products serve and write them into the system as personas. Then count what already exists."
        },
        {
          "title": "Tokens",
          "text": "The foundations as named values: colour, type, space, shape, chosen for those people.",
          "group": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Components",
          "text": "The most-used parts first, built from the tokens.",
          "group": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Guidelines and site",
          "text": "The rules next to each component, on a site everyone can search."
        },
        {
          "title": "Adopted",
          "text": "One product moves first, the rest follow, and a check catches drift.",
          "end": true
        }
      ],
      "alt": {
        "label": "The style-guide route",
        "steps": [
          "A PDF of rules",
          "Teams copy what they can",
          "Drift by the next release"
        ],
        "note": "A style guide describes; a design system is used, in design files and in code."
      }
    },
